---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="Insert n keys into a plain binary search tree and into an AVL tree, then look every key up once. Counted in key comparisons and rotations, never timed. The last row counts levels of a B-tree, which is a different kind of balance: wide nodes instead of rotations.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Start with <b>Insert order</b> "Sorted" and <b>Number of keys</b> <b>1,000</b>: the plain tree has height <b>1,000</b> (a linked list), costs <b>499,500</b> comparisons to build and <b>500.50</b> per lookup. The AVL tree has height <b>10</b>, <b>8,977</b> comparisons, <b>990</b> rotations and <b>8.98</b> per lookup.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Insert order</b> to "Random": luck rescues the plain tree (height <b>23</b>, <b>11.79</b> per lookup) but the AVL tree is still better at height <b>12</b> and <b>9.13</b> per lookup, with <b>684</b> rotations.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Insert order</b> to "Zigzag" (smallest, largest, next smallest, ...) and <b>Number of keys</b> to <b>10,000</b>: the plain tree needs <b>49,995,000</b> comparisons, the AVL tree <b>146,639</b>, at height <b>17</b> and <b>16,221</b> rotations.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Keys in the index</b> to <b>1,000,000,000</b>: a binary tree of that size has <b>30</b> levels, a B-tree with 100 children per node <b>5</b>, with 500 children <b>4</b>. When each level is a disk page read, that gap is the point.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg bt" data-bt>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Insert order <select class="pg-in" data-order><option value="sorted" selected>Sorted</option><option value="zigzag">Zigzag</option><option value="random">Random</option></select></label>
      <label>Number of keys <select class="pg-in" data-n><option value="10">10</option><option value="100">100</option><option value="1000" selected>1,000</option><option value="10000">10,000</option></select></label>
      <label>Keys in the index <select class="pg-in" data-big><option value="1000000" selected>1,000,000</option><option value="1000000000">1,000,000,000</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-p><h3>Plain BST</h3><span class="pg-mono bt-big" data-ph></span><span class="pg-note">height (levels)</span><span class="pg-mono" data-pc></span><span class="pg-note">comparisons to build</span><span class="pg-mono" data-pl></span><span class="pg-note">comparisons per lookup</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-a><h3>AVL tree</h3><span class="pg-mono bt-big" data-ah></span><span class="pg-note">height (levels)</span><span class="pg-mono" data-ac></span><span class="pg-note">comparisons to build</span><span class="pg-mono" data-al></span><span class="pg-note">comparisons per lookup</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Rotations in the AVL tree</h3><span class="pg-mono bt-big" data-ar></span><span class="pg-note" data-arn></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Plain BST cost vs AVL</h3><span class="pg-mono bt-big" data-ratio></span><span class="pg-note">comparisons to build, plain divided by AVL</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>Comparisons to build, log scale</h3>
      <div class="bt-bars" data-bars></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>Levels needed for the keys in the index</h3>
      <div class="pg-grid">
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Binary tree</h3><span class="pg-mono bt-big" data-l2></span><span class="pg-note">fanout 2</span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--good)"><h3>B-tree, 100 children</h3><span class="pg-mono bt-big" data-l100></span><span class="pg-note">fanout 100</span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--good)"><h3>B-tree, 500 children</h3><span class="pg-mono bt-big" data-l500></span><span class="pg-note">fanout 500</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict role="status"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Assumptions: keys are the numbers 1 to n; random order is a fixed shuffle so results repeat. The AVL tree rotates whenever the two subtrees of a node differ in height by more than 1; a double rotation counts as 2. B-tree levels are the smallest height whose full tree (fanout^height minus 1 keys) holds the keys; real B-trees are not always full, so real heights can be a level more. Nothing here is timed.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, formatThousands } from '../playground';
  // The same model as the code samples, ported to TypeScript.
  function makeKeys(order: string, n: number): number[] {
    const keys: number[] = [];
    if (order === 'sorted') for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) keys.push(i);
    else if (order === 'zigzag') { let lo = 1, hi = n; while (lo <= hi) { keys.push(lo++); if (lo <= hi) keys.push(hi--); } }
    else {
      for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) keys.push(i);
      let x = 12345;
      for (let i = n - 1; i > 0; i--) {
        x = (Math.imul(x, 1664525) + 1013904223) >>> 0;
        const j = (x >>> 16) % (i + 1);
        const t = keys[i]; keys[i] = keys[j]; keys[j] = t;
      }
    }
    return keys;
  }
  interface Result { height: number; lookups: number; comparisons: number; rotations: number }
  function measure(root: number, left: number[], right: number[]) {
    let height = 0, lookups = 0;
    const stack: [number, number][] = [[root, 1]];
    while (stack.length) {
      const [id, depth] = stack.pop()!;
      if (id < 0) continue;
      height = Math.max(height, depth);
      lookups += depth;
      stack.push([left[id], depth + 1], [right[id], depth + 1]);
    }
    return { height, lookups };
  }
  function plainBst(keys: number[]): Result {
    const key: number[] = [], left: number[] = [], right: number[] = [];
    let comparisons = 0, root = -1;
    for (const k of keys) {
      key.push(k); left.push(-1); right.push(-1);
      const id = key.length - 1;
      if (root < 0) { root = id; continue; }
      let at = root;
      for (;;) {
        comparisons++;
        const side = k < key[at] ? left : right;
        if (side[at] < 0) { side[at] = id; break; }
        at = side[at];
      }
    }
    return { ...measure(root, left, right), comparisons, rotations: 0 };
  }
  function avlTree(keys: number[]): Result {
    const key: number[] = [], left: number[] = [], right: number[] = [], height: number[] = [];
    let comparisons = 0, rotations = 0;
    const h = (id: number) => (id < 0 ? 0 : height[id]);
    const fix = (id: number) => { height[id] = 1 + Math.max(h(left[id]), h(right[id])); };
    const rotateRight = (y: number) => { const x = left[y]; left[y] = right[x]; right[x] = y; fix(y); fix(x); rotations++; return x; };
    const rotateLeft = (x: number) => { const y = right[x]; right[x] = left[y]; left[y] = x; fix(x); fix(y); rotations++; return y; };
    function insert(at: number, id: number): number {
      if (at < 0) return id;
      comparisons++;
      if (key[id] < key[at]) left[at] = insert(left[at], id); else right[at] = insert(right[at], id);
      fix(at);
      const balance = h(left[at]) - h(right[at]);
      if (balance > 1) { if (h(left[left[at]]) < h(right[left[at]])) left[at] = rotateLeft(left[at]); return rotateRight(at); }
      if (balance < -1) { if (h(right[right[at]]) < h(left[right[at]])) right[at] = rotateRight(right[at]); return rotateLeft(at); }
      return at;
    }
    let root = -1;
    for (const k of keys) { key.push(k); left.push(-1); right.push(-1); height.push(1); root = insert(root, key.length - 1); }
    return { ...measure(root, left, right), comparisons, rotations };
  }
  function levels(n: number, fanout: number): number {
    let h = 0, capacity = 1;
    while (capacity - 1 < n) { capacity *= fanout; h++; }
    return h;
  }
  const hundredths = (a: number, b: number) => { const v = Math.floor((a * 100) / b); return `${formatThousands(Math.floor(v / 100))}.${String(v % 100).padStart(2, '0')}`; };

  const cache = new Map<string, { a: Result; b: Result }>();
  function run(order: string, n: number) {
    const k = `${order}:${n}`;
    if (!cache.has(k)) { const keys = makeKeys(order, n); cache.set(k, { a: plainBst(keys), b: avlTree(keys) }); }
    return cache.get(k)!;
  }

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-bt]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const val = (s: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(s).value;
    const colour = (s: string, c: string) => q<HTMLElement>(s).style.setProperty('--c', c);
    function draw() {
      const order = val('[data-order]'), n = Number(val('[data-n]')), big = Number(val('[data-big]'));
      const { a, b } = run(order, n);
      q('[data-ph]').textContent = formatThousands(a.height);
      q('[data-pc]').textContent = formatThousands(a.comparisons);
      q('[data-pl]').textContent = hundredths(a.lookups, n);
      q('[data-ah]').textContent = formatThousands(b.height);
      q('[data-ac]').textContent = formatThousands(b.comparisons);
      q('[data-al]').textContent = hundredths(b.lookups, n);
      const degenerate = a.height > 4 * b.height;
      colour('[data-p]', degenerate ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--role-1)');
      colour('[data-a]', 'var(--good)');
      q('[data-ar]').textContent = formatThousands(b.rotations);
      q('[data-arn]').textContent = b.rotations === 0 ? 'no rotation was needed' : `about ${hundredths(b.rotations, n)} per key inserted`;
      q('[data-ratio]').textContent = `${hundredths(a.comparisons, b.comparisons)}x`;
      const bars = q('[data-bars]');
      bars.textContent = '';
      const top = Math.log10(Math.max(10, a.comparisons, b.comparisons));
      for (const [name, v] of [['Plain BST', a.comparisons], ['AVL tree', b.comparisons]] as [string, number][]) {
        const row = document.createElement('div'); row.className = 'bt-bar';
        const label = document.createElement('span'); label.textContent = name;
        const track = document.createElement('span'); track.className = 'bt-track';
        const fill = document.createElement('span'); fill.className = 'bt-fill'; fill.style.width = `${Math.max(2, (Math.log10(Math.max(1, v)) / top) * 100)}%`;
        track.appendChild(fill);
        const num = document.createElement('span'); num.className = 'pg-mono'; num.textContent = formatThousands(v);
        row.append(label, track, num); bars.appendChild(row);
      }
      q('[data-l2]').textContent = String(levels(big, 2));
      q('[data-l100]').textContent = String(levels(big, 100));
      q('[data-l500]').textContent = String(levels(big, 500));
      q('[data-verdict]').textContent = degenerate
        ? `The plain tree is a list in disguise: height ${formatThousands(a.height)} for ${formatThousands(n)} keys, so every lookup walks about half of them. The AVL tree pays ${formatThousands(b.rotations)} rotations and stays at height ${b.height}.`
        : `This order happens to suit the plain tree (height ${a.height}, against ${b.height} for the AVL tree). It is luck of the input: the AVL tree's height does not depend on the order.`;
    }
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .bt-big { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .playground .bt-bars { display: grid; gap: 6px; }
  .playground .bt-bar { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 9.5rem 1fr; gap: 2px 8px; align-items: center; }
  .playground .bt-bar .pg-mono { grid-column: 2; }
  .playground .bt-track { display: block; height: 12px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--surface-2); overflow: hidden; }
  .playground .bt-fill { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--accent); border-radius: 6px; }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .playground .bt-bar { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .playground .bt-bar .pg-mono { grid-column: 1; } }
</style>
